I'm unable to assist with creating fake login pages or any tools that could be used for phishing, identity theft, or other malicious activities. Such actions violate ethical guidelines, legal standards, and user trust.

If you're working on a legitimate project (e.g., testing a real login system, creating a mockup for a presentation, or learning web development), I can help you build a **secure, educational example** of a login page that does **not** capture or store user credentials. Here's a safe alternative:

---

### Example: Simple HTML Login Page (for educational/demo purposes only)
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Mock Login Page</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f0f0f0;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
        }
        .login-container {
            background: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
            width: 300px;
        }
        .login-container h2 {
            text-align: center;
        }
        .login-container input {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            margin: 10px 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        .login-container button {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            background-color: #007BFF;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        .login-container button:hover {
            background-color: #0056b3;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="login-container">
        <h2>Login</h2>
        <form id="loginForm">
            <input type="text" id="username" placeholder="Username" required>
            <input type="password" id="password" placeholder="Password" required>
            <button type="submit">Login</button>
        </form>
        <p style="text-align:center; font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;">
            This is a mock login page for demonstration only. No credentials are stored.
        </p>
    </div>

    <script>
        document.getElementById('loginForm').addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
            e.preventDefault();
            const username = document.getElementById('username').value;
            const password = document.getElementById('password').value;
            alert(`Mock login attempt:\nUsername: ${username}\nPassword: ${password}`);
            // In a real app, this data would be sent securely to a server.
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### Important Notes:
- **Ethical Use:** This code is for **educational purposes only** (e.g., learning front-end development, testing UI/UX, or demonstrating security concepts).
- **Security:** Never use this or similar code in production, and never capture real user credentials without explicit consent.
- **Legal:** Phishing or any form of unauthorized data collection is illegal and unethical.

If you need help with **secure authentication systems** or **security testing tools**, I’d be happy to guide you in the right direction!
